 "unit": "sk-thm-br",
 "title": "Flat ring maps satisfy going down",
 "statement": "Let $R\\to S$ be a flat homomorphism of commutative rings [def-weil-pbc-flat-ring-map]. Then it has the going-down property: whenever $\\mathfrak p_1\\subseteq\\mathfrak p_2$ are prime ideals of $R$ and $\\mathfrak q_2$ is a prime ideal of $S$ with contraction $\\mathfrak p_2$, there is a prime $\\mathfrak q_1\\subseteq\\mathfrak q_2$ whose contraction is $\\mathfrak p_1$.",
 "source": {
